{
  "_about": "The companion's faces: what its screen draws. One source for Blender (make_face_textures.py) and for the app and the website (companion.js draws the same shapes on a canvas). Shapes are in screen-width units, x to the right and y up, measured from the eye centre or the mouth centre. An eye shape is drawn for the left eye and mirrored for the right unless 'mirror' is false. Shape kinds: line (points), curve (start, corner, end), ellipse (c, r), spiral, path (a start point, then points to go straight to, or [corner x, corner y, x, y] to curve to; 'fill' closes and fills it). 'cut': true takes the shape away from what is already drawn (the dark line of a tongue inside a glowing mouth). First copied from the locked sheets (2026-10-02); made bigger and cuter on Dee's word, 2026-10-03: 'i need big eyes and more cute things ... a little big mouth looking cute with expressions'.",
